[{"id":"VRCE-2-45-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":45,"verse":1,"english":"As for the purpose of protecting his brother, Lakṣmaṇa was watching him out of sincere affection, Guha burning in grief addressed that descendant of Raghu, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-51-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2045001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"969a12c29fc0a665808a78026333a7537a65ec7d6e262ecc5e685b46c5b74ebe","compact":"b466d1dbd40bede2f24cca357f400c4289f83beddc446abb7b6a58596d50f882","nasal":"fe21f5af9e800afd7640f4fa4f2239036533214d5f0c3c1f9d823f29898737dd"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-45-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":45,"verse":2,"english":"This O child, is the easeful bed that has been prepared for you. O prince, do you as you listen, lie down upon it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-51-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2045002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4415a6f0b7cc462076c2415699efd98795d59cf0c723344774e0d2ddfcd846ec","compact":"c560ba75fa1e2d1347a8c7fdd24f918bbb508d973affe7cc7f44118db664154d","nasal":"c560ba75fa1e2d1347a8c7fdd24f918bbb508d973affe7cc7f44118db664154d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-45-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":45,"verse":3,"english":"These (foresters) are inured to this hardship; but you are worthy of ease. We will wake up during the night for guarding Kākutstha.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-51-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2045003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bbbe033d02f3c52a146770585c8f9905433851cecbc657f5c813df3dbb54b52b","compact":"4d764ba0e2b3ca8c83563e669f5fa24cdfacf37cb0bc59c833d8c5956245e123","nasal":"4d764ba0e2b3ca8c83563e669f5fa24cdfacf37cb0bc59c833d8c5956245e123"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-45-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":45,"verse":4,"english":"There is none on earth dearer to me than Răma. This I tell you truly and I swear by truth itself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.534,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-51-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2045004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e0c05d0f0a0feb4dfd7400c6edf9011b88085fe18d79671524dc02854ca2c4ed","compact":"ba7b247cf79827c4097b70284be8598c2aec978b85f8c36dcf3c0753e10b9e7d","nasal":"ba7b247cf79827c4097b70284be8598c2aec978b85f8c36dcf3c0753e10b9e7d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-45-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":45,"verse":5,"english":"Through his grace I hope in this world to attain high fame, and great religious merit as well as completely secure profit and pleasure.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.647,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-51-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2045005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1b58a4f8660ab10d58a322af26e20f7e6dd257da1464c40dbbf297d425d138b5","compact":"456eb6c04675747efe1b9ad1db3abccd1f8f5d9d4a730d556797586ae6159158","nasal":"456eb6c04675747efe1b9ad1db3abccd1f8f5d9d4a730d556797586ae6159158"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-45-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":45,"verse":6,"english":"I will bow in hand in company with my kindred adequately guard my dear friend reposing with Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.847,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-51-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2045006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0e8b66693063a241e52a2da1f91706a85bb3400a7be3cab5133aba8c0b463741","compact":"7df468c602f55ad69fe78ff0e5d7979465038926e41c30fcb14a7e6c20c6154e","nasal":"7df468c602f55ad69fe78ff0e5d7979465038926e41c30fcb14a7e6c20c6154e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-45-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":45,"verse":7,"english":"Always ranging in this forest, nothing herein is unknown to me. I shall vanquish even any mighty body of fourfold forces (that may come up against us.)","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.559,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-51-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2045007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e8195c854ffd2fa0ca2f7993a1075348bce3201c222fda09eb48719d61e65d2b","compact":"01d21adcf0162821515ea48621e06f91ace5c3ab04a54bac4cd9b6ffdfdb9a01","nasal":"ed6db5ab0964f6142b8c5f0bebcaeb828af03fc497e4b835c9789e303f0d607b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-45-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":45,"verse":8,"english":"Thereupon Laksmana said, O sinless one, protected by you ever having your sight fixed on virtue, we do not fear to live in this place. But how with Dasaratha's son lying down on the ground along with Sītă can I indulge in sleep or what is the use of my living and enjoying happiness?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-51-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2045008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"84354b6c1c6bb24c2ee2bad6b034c5e85b7dba7bea9610bac597011077601285","compact":"cba0e3b8cefbdfb6db337cccd996276446a34d18330e6461f6839ccfe4b01c26","nasal":"cba0e3b8cefbdfb6db337cccd996276446a34d18330e6461f6839ccfe4b01c26"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-45-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":45,"verse":9,"english":"Thereupon Laksmana said, O sinless one, protected by you ever having your sight fixed on virtue, we do not fear to live in this place. But how with Dasaratha's son lying down on the ground along with Sītă can I indulge in sleep or what is the use of my living and enjoying happiness?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-51-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2045009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a3920034b6f94a6228fd76457c37753445b1866f490a23927d78d40d734fb582","compact":"6cb86ccbffdc5fc1a466adebfa6a869147ca837f72f37e55876b5a746826e322","nasal":"6cb86ccbffdc5fc1a466adebfa6a869147ca837f72f37e55876b5a746826e322"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-45-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":45,"verse":10,"english":"Him do you behold with ease asleep on the grass in company with Sītā, who was incapable of being borne in fight by the gods and the Asuras, and who obtained through Mantras and austerities and various endeavours, Dasaratha crowned with every auspicious mark, is the most meritorious son of the king. Rāma being banished, the king will not live long and the earth will shortly be widowed.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.797,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-51-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2045010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e962ec11cb106af8786411b4679ef36dd8e983f4c1abeeaf0d2deee2d3f8d2dd","compact":"f7ade92883fc0aa842c9d3ce8a1e4b1e4d2488dbaf1e8d3dc58df0f54ebbd1bf","nasal":"f7ade92883fc0aa842c9d3ce8a1e4b1e4d2488dbaf1e8d3dc58df0f54ebbd1bf"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-45-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":45,"verse":11,"english":"Him do you behold with ease asleep on the grass in company with Sītā, who was incapable of being borne in fight by the gods and the Asuras, and who obtained through Mantras and austerities and various endeavours, Dasaratha crowned with every auspicious mark, is the most meritorious son of the king. Rāma being banished, the king will not live long and the earth will shortly be widowed.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-51-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2045011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6b9549938398e20b249c55b2d6450b194a0a51a07a8d3b1eb97bc4b7c46f166e","compact":"367689971585ee40e90290e0f06b8de42055a1addd56a40c4476985b607ef4fb","nasal":"2a321ca5d581faeaee170cc2c851f6473ccd83c2bff302275d0bdb8a138b2494"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-45-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":45,"verse":12,"english":"Him do you behold with ease asleep on the grass in company with Sītā, who was incapable of being borne in fight by the gods and the Asuras, and who obtained through Mantras and austerities and various endeavours, Dasaratha crowned with every auspicious mark, is the most meritorious son of the king. Rāma being banished, the king will not live long and the earth will shortly be widowed.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-51-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2045012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a8216a82477e1fff53ce8b5f1df594da2b6754351326a5d6234ced9215e2ed11","compact":"6925b1ddb287b7184f816d0ff826275674513c4c8fc03cca89ccb74f386949b5","nasal":"6925b1ddb287b7184f816d0ff826275674513c4c8fc03cca89ccb74f386949b5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-45-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":45,"verse":13,"english":"Having bewailed aloud, the women have, methinks, (by this time) ceased through fatigue, and the king's residence is still.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-51-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2045013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a97d2b9e389d893f7005285888e3d36e07e381d1fc758b7e5